WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.620
- All right, let's wind things down

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.960
with something simply
beautiful and inspirational

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.400
from the pages of social media.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.500
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.450
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.350
You may know

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.380
that I'm a bit obsessed with
all things under the sea.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.420
So I love what one scientist is doing

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.240
to give us lay people a
glimpse of the delicate lives

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.490
of turtles living in our oceans.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:23.280
He temporarily mounts
cameras to turtle shells

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:26.670
as they swim, interact,
and eat beneath the water.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.890
Not only does it produce stunning visuals.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.050
I love this video so much, it's so happy.

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:33.900
It reinforces just how
delicate marine life is

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.920
and how simple it is

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.650
for us to do our part
to protect ocean life.

00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.060
From the Turtle Camera Project,

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.230
everybody say hello to
Dr. Nathan Robinson!

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.883
(audience cheering and applauding)

00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:46.320
- Hi, everyone. Hi, Kelly.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:47.700
- Hello, Dr. Robinson!

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.260
This is so beautiful.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:50.490
I just love the footage so much.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.510
It makes you so happy.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.343
It's so good.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:53.790
So how did you come up with this idea?

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:55.740
- Oh, well, it all
started several years ago.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:58.200
I was working on a research
vessel in Costa Rica

00:00:58.200 --> 00:00:59.910
and I discovered a sea turtle

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.260
that had a something led
wedged inside its nostril.

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:06.660
And when I grabbed and
I jumped into action.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:08.940
Grabbed my (indistinct) I
have to pull out the object,

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.980
I discovered that it was a plastic straw.

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:14.640
In fact, it was this plastic straw.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:17.100
When that video was uploaded online,

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.960
immediately went viral.

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.570
And engaged with millions
of people worldwide

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:24.030
about the issue that single use plastics

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:25.860
are having on our oceans.

00:01:25.860 --> 00:01:28.530
And seeing that impact
filled me with inspiration

00:01:28.530 --> 00:01:31.350
to start wondering what
other videos I could produce

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:33.990
to help engaging with
ever larger audiences

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:36.030
about ocean conservation.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:39.090
And one of my next big projects
was the Turtle Cam Project.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:39.923
- I love this.

00:01:39.923 --> 00:01:41.730
So how do the cameras work?

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:43.380
Like what have you learned?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:45.480
- So this is a Turtle Cam.

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.580
It's a dive camera.

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:50.280
And we temporarily mount
onto a sea turtle shell

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:51.540
using these metal links

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.150
that corroded after about
three to four hours.

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.200
So when the corrode,

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.790
the camera pops off,

00:01:56.790 --> 00:02:00.390
we're able to find the camera
again using this antenna.

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.090
And that's where we
recover the footage inside.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.370
And that footage gives
us wonderful insights

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.010
into where sea turtles living,

00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.600
what they're feeding on.

00:02:09.600 --> 00:02:11.700
But it's also given us
some amazing insights

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.290
into their social lives.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:15.150
But the most important
thing that we've learned

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:17.970
through all of these videos,

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:22.680
is the impact that each one of
us can have on ocean health.

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:23.700
Simple decisions,

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.860
reducing your CO2 output,

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:28.560
reducing the amount of
plastic you consume.

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:29.730
These are the little steps

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.980
that we can make wherever
we live in the world

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:35.040
to make our oceans a
healthier place for ourselves

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.900
and all the animals that live there.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:37.860
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.390
Well, thank you so much, Nathan.

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.550
I'm liking your posts right now.

00:02:41.550 --> 00:02:42.383
Well, that's not all.

00:02:42.383 --> 00:02:43.890
Our season long partner pilot pin,

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:44.730
Makers of Friction,

00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:47.100
the go to erasable pin of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:48.690
want to celebrate those creating

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:51.210
and inspiring fearlessly
just like you, sir.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:52.680
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.349
Maybe buy more cameras.
(audience cheering)

00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:56.350
(Kelly chuckling)

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.893
- That is, oh my God, that's amazing.

00:02:58.893 --> 00:02:59.947
Thank you so much.

00:02:59.947 --> 00:03:01.470
- Absolutely.
(inaudible)

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:03.090
- Such an incredible gesture.

00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:06.210
That will go to help protect
sea turtles worldwide.

00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:07.920
- Ah man, keep going what you're doing.

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.900
We love it and we supporting it.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:11.370
So keep what you're doing Dr. Robinson.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:13.058
Thank you so much for joining us.

00:03:13.058 --> 00:03:13.891
(audience cheering)

00:03:13.891 --> 00:03:15.540
Thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:18.060
Kristen Bell, (inaudible), Candace Nelson,

